---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Terms of Service Page
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — December"
  description="Terms of Service for December software, CLI, and cloud execution."
  canonicalUrl="https://trydecember.com/terms"
  activePath="/terms"
  hideHeader={false}
  hideFooter={false}
>
  <!-- Main Container: Identical horizontal gap/margins to landing page and docs page -->
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[940px] px-6 sm:px-8 md:px-10 lg:px-12 pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12 sm:pb-24 min-w-0">
    <!-- Breadcrumb Navigation Bar -->
    <nav class="flex items-center flex-wrap font-mono text-xs text-[#64748b] mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#090a0f] transition-colors">home</a>
        <span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#64748b]">legal</span>
        <span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#090a0f] font-medium">[terms]</span>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- Article Layout: Spans full width matching landing page & docs structure -->
    <article class="w-full min-w-0">
      <!-- Document Header -->
      <header class="mb-8 max-w-3xl min-w-0">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs text-[#64748b] mb-2">Effective: September 2026</div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-[#090a0f] leading-snug">
          Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-sm sm:text-[15px] text-[#52525b] leading-relaxed">
          These Terms of Service govern your access to and use of December software, command-line interfaces,
          and cloud execution environments provided by Phasehumans Inc.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Markdown / Body Content -->
      <div class="docs-prose min-w-0 max-w-full text-[#52525b] text-sm sm:text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2>Acceptance & Eligibility</h2>
          <p>
            By downloading, installing, running, or accessing December (including the CLI, desktop companions,
            web applications, and cloud sandbox services), you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you are
            entering into these Terms on behalf of a company or other legal entity, you represent that you have
            the authority to bind such entity. If you do not agree to these terms, you must immediately cease use.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>License & Permitted Use</h2>
          <p>
            Subject to your compliance with these Terms, Phasehumans grants you a revocable, non-exclusive,
            non-transferable, limited right to install and use December to develop, test, debug, and deploy
            your software applications. Open-source components are governed by their respective licenses.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Code Ownership & IP</h2>
          <p>
            Your code belongs to you. Phasehumans does not assert any ownership, copyright, patent, or
            proprietary interest in your source code, repositories, prompts, or generated outputs. You retain
            all right, title, and interest in content you provide. Generated code outputs are assigned to you
            upon generation. We do not use your private code or prompts to train AI models.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Subscriptions & BYOK</h2>
          <p>
            December provides local workstation execution and optional cloud infrastructure.
            When using your own API keys (BYOK), fees are billed directly to your provider account with no
            intermediary markup. Cloud sandbox features are billed per your subscription plan or pay-as-you-go
            rates. Subscriptions may be cancelled at any time and take effect at the end of the billing cycle.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Cloud Sandboxes</h2>
          <p>
            Cloud handoff provisions an isolated micro-VM with dedicated CPU, RAM, and root filesystem to execute
            commands and build artifacts. Preview URLs are routed over TLS 1.3. You are responsible for securing
            any public preview URLs and ensuring sensitive credentials are not exposed through public endpoints.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>
          <p>You agree not to use December or its cloud sandboxes to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Develop, generate, or execute malware, ransomware, or malicious exploits.</li>
            <li>Conduct unauthorized penetration tests or denial-of-service attacks.</li>
            <li>Circumvent security sandboxing, rate limits, or isolation barriers.</li>
            <li>Mine cryptocurrency or run unauthorized distributed workloads.</li>
            <li>Violate applicable export control laws and regulations.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Warranty Disclaimers</h2>
          <p>
            December is provided &ldquo;as-is&rdquo; without warranties of any kind, express or implied.
            AI models may produce incorrect code or hallucinated outputs — you are solely responsible for
            reviewing and verifying all code before production use. To the maximum extent permitted by law,
            Phasehumans shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Governing Law & Contact</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, United States. We reserve the right
            to modify these Terms with reasonable advance notice. For questions or enterprise agreements,
            contact us at <a href="mailto:team@trydecember.com">team@trydecember.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Navigation & Contact -->
      <div class="mt-14 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
        <span class="text-[#64748b]">
          Questions? <a href="mailto:team@trydecember.com" class="text-[#87b2f4] hover:underline">team@trydecember.com</a>
        </span>
        <a
          href="/privacy"
          class="group inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 p-2.5 border border-[#e2e8f0] bg-white hover:border-[#87b2f4] text-[#090a0f] transition-all"
        >
          <span>Privacy Policy</span>
          <span class="text-[#94a3b8] group-hover:text-[#87b2f4] transition-colors">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
